<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Dec 28.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Dec 28.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Dec 28 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Dec 22-Dec 28</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,125,640 tns	115,053 tns    10.22 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 816,579 tns	 83,582 tns    10.24 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,092,551 tns	104,946 tns     9.61 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to Dec 28</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     4,563,303 tns	431,225 tns     9.45 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     3,700,755 tns	330,419 tns     8.93 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     4,197,348 tns	384,504 tns     9.16 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 44 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 47 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 47 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530.  E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com))</p>
